-- title:
--   Correctness of the truncated band-length procedure
-- statement:
--   Fix a program, resource limits, a call depth, and an initial memory $\mu$. Suppose the designated procedure contains the band-length body. Let $n,g,i\in\mathbb N$ satisfy $g>0$ and $ig\le n$, and suppose the word-magnitude limit is at least $n+g+4$. Invoked with arguments $(n,g,i)$, the procedure terminates within $80$ steps and returns a value $r$ and memory $\nu$ satisfying
--
--   $$r=\min\{g,n-ig\},\qquad\nu=\mu.$$
--
--   This contract supplies the exact length of a possibly truncated final band for weighted-score calls while preserving the input memory.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/c0ldzy17/three-sum-lean/blob/2b639655e07421b9ac743de9090459bab473a7c0/Submission/ThreeSum/LightBandWeightedScoreSlice.lean#L21-L41

